    "summary": "Textile: composed of six narrow strip woven cotton lengths hand sewn together selvedge to selvedge. Plain weave: dyed yellow and black cotton warps: dyed yellow and orange wefts. This creates yellow and black warp stripes crossed by black weft stripes at either end. The combination of different coloured warps and wefts creates different shades of the initial colours i.e. yellow and orange creates a warm rich yellow.",
